**Resubmitted: deviation (T4C), preferred level.**

Change from the prior submission: the inserted clause is now explicitly numbered **§ 11.3 "Termination for Convenience"** (previously an out-of-scheme "11.2A"), so Section 11's numbering and cross-referencing scheme stays consistent. Validation returned `ok:true` with minimality clean.

Operative content (unchanged in substance, all four preferred elements in one paragraph):
- Corio may terminate this Agreement for convenience — element 1 (no Order Form / partial-termination language added, as none exists here);
- on thirty (30) days' prior written notice — element 2;
- Commerce One refunds prepaid fees pro rata for the post-termination period — element 3;
- Commerce One has no convenience termination right during the initial five-year term or any renewal term — element 4.

Nothing is deleted: § 11.1 term/auto-renewal and § 11.2 breach and insolvency exits remain verbatim, and no "notwithstanding" override was added pre-emptively. The fallback (60–90 days' notice with a three-month fee cap) is offered in the negotiation comment only.
